 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the real property tax law, in relation to limiting the shift\nbetween classes of taxable property in the town of Haverstraw, county of\nRockland",
    "basePrintNo": "S5233",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S5233-2025",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §1903, RPT L",
    "lawSection": "Real Property Tax Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S5233\n\nSPONSOR: WEBER\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the real property tax law, in relation to limiting the\nshift between classes of taxable property in the town of Haverstraw,\ncounty of Rockland\n\n \nPURPOSE:,\n\nThis bill would limit shifts between homestead and non-homestead proper-\nty classes of no more than one percent per year\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1: Amends section 1903 of the real property tax law as It\nrelates to limiting the shift between dasses of taxable property to one\npercent in the Town of Haverstraw in Rockland County.\n\nSection 2: Provides the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nMunicipalities with classes of taxable property (homestead/non-\nhomestead) often face drastic fluctuations in shifts between the two\nclasses of taxable property. Current law limits those shifts at five\npercent but this bill would restrict the shift in the Town of Haverstraw\nto no more than one percent to create stability in the tax base from\nyear to year. Similar legislation was proposed and Implemented in prior\nyears and this act will extend the limitation in the Town of Haverstraw\nfor another year.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
    "multiSponsors": {
